  "distinctnessReading": "A3 §2 distinctness is keyed on (hardSeat, gameSha256): two seat-mirrored games with identical action sequences are two experiments, not one, so a cleanly mirrored cell is not invalid by construction. Pair-level distinctness — the sampling unit every Elo interval is computed over — is unchanged and keys on the pair's two game hashes together, so a replicated PAIR (A2's failure mode) still counts once. Both counts are reported per cell: distinctGames (seat-keyed, gates cellValid) and distinctGameSequences (hash only, report-only).",
